&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2714&quot; title=&quot;Cleanup GridOffHeapPartitionedMap when cache is destroyed&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-2714&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-2714&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Cleanup GridOffHeapPartitionedMap when cache is destroyed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15496495" author="amartianov" created="Fri, 16 Sep 2016 14:46:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I fixed problem with unremoved GridOffHeapPartitionedMap. This fix is actual for ONHEAP_TIERED and OFFHEAP_TIERED memory modes.&lt;br/&gt;
But found out another bug: if cache is created with memory mode OFFHEAP_VALUES then offheap memory is processed in another way and isn&apos;t freed after cache destroy.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15506686" author="sboikov" created="Tue, 20 Sep 2016 14:18:04 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks Andrey, I merged current fix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But let&apos;s also fix leak for OFFHEAP_VALUES mode: now there is only one way to clear memory: iterate over all entries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15516168" author="amartianov" created="Fri, 23 Sep 2016 11:24:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I added clearing of offheap memory at cache destroy in OFFHEAP_VALUES mode and updated PR.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15516739" author="amartianov" created="Fri, 23 Sep 2016 15:21:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;TC tests passed. Please review.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15532755" author="sboikov" created="Thu, 29 Sep 2016 13:19:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Andrey,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I reviewed your fix for offheap_values cleanup, have one comment: potentially there can be lots of entries and it is better to do cleanup in parallel from multiple threads. For dht cache each cache partition can be processed independently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also for better test coverage please add test with two nodes, and make sure test creates entries in both near and dht caches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15958723" author="sboikov" created="Thu, 6 Apr 2017 10:50:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Is not relevant anymore with new PageMemory architecture.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
